<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Eohippus angustidens Schnakenberg wavelength at 78 µm (Wasatchian, 52.0 Ma) (Eohippus angustidens)",
        "Eohippus angustidens Schnakenberg wavelength at 78 µm (Wasatchian, 52.0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eohippus angustidens morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eohippus angustidens specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eohippus angustidens" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a fossil of Eohippus angustidens preserves a measured 78 µm pigment stripe.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery plate is a histological section.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: D_u and D_v are solved so k_c equals 2 pi / 7.752e-05 m at ratio 8.22. Those diffusivities are not taken from an equid epidermis table.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The GIF last frame is a 0.72-weight blend of the saturated field and the gallery plate in pass 1.",
        "reported_in_source: MacFadden 1986 and Froehlich 2002 place Eohippus at the start of the equid body-size series and split the early Eocene genera.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981 give the dispersion relation and k_c formula used here.",
        "transfer_boundary: Cellular lambda_c is treated as conserved from Eohippus (52.0 Ma) to Orohippus (48 Ma anchor) because it is set by cell-biological D and kinetics. Organ-scale stripe count is not." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eohippus angustidens (Early Eocene (Wasatchian, 52.0 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eohippus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eohippus angustidens; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981 give the dispersion relation and k_c formula used here. | MacFadden 1986 and Froehlich 2002 place Eohippus at the start of the equid body-size series and split the early Eocene genera.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u and D_v are solved so k_c equals 2 pi / 7.752e-05 m at ratio 8.22. Those diffusivities are not taken from an equid epidermis table. | The GIF last frame is a 0.72-weight blend of the saturated field and the gallery plate in pass 1.; transfer_boundary: Cellular lambda_c is treated as conserved from Eohippus (52.0 Ma) to Orohippus (48 Ma anchor) because it is set by cell-biological D and kinetics. Organ-scale stripe count is not.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a fossil of Eohippus angustidens preserves a measured 78 µm pigment stripe. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a histological section.]; phenomenon_size: 66 µm (6.596e-05 m, log10=-4.181 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 66 µm to 14.8 cm): 66 µm:eohippus-angustidens-bioelectric-polarity, 206 µm:eohippus-angustidens-vertex-packing, 3.3 mm:eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength, 6.6 mm:eohippus-angustidens-clock-wavefront, 1.5 cm:eohippus-angustidens-morphogen-condensation, 1.8 cm:eohippus-angustidens-elastic-buckling, 2.1 cm:eohippus-angustidens-flux-canalization, 2.9 cm:eohippus-angustidens-branching-tree" ;
